# Context filter for builds whose context is this repo root — the default node build
# (docker-compose.yaml: `context: .`, dockerfile `go/Dockerfile`) and any ad-hoc
# `docker build .` here.
#
# Two ignore files cover that build and they are alternatives, not layers: BuildKit looks for
# <dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile, finds go/Dockerfile.dockerignore, and uses
# it *instead* of this file — the two are never merged. This file is what applies when no
# per-Dockerfile ignore file is honoured: the legacy builder (DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0) reads only a
# context-root .dockerignore and would otherwise send this whole working copy, .env files
# included, to the daemon and into a layer. It also applies to any dockerfile that has no
# sibling ignore file of its own. So both files have to be complete on their own; keep them
# in step.
#
# Exclusions here are not just about build speed. Everything left in the context is handed to
# the daemon, is eligible to land in a layer through a wide COPY, and contributes to the layer
# hashes the reproducible build depends on. go/Dockerfile copies only go/go.mod, go/go.sum,
# go/cmd/, go/internal/ and go/pkg/, so nothing outside those needs to be in the context.
#
# Patterns are matched against paths relative to the context root, and `*` does not cross `/`
# — a bare `foo` matches only a top-level foo, `**/foo` matches it at any depth.

# Private keys and credentials. .env* covers the templates too (an image never needs them),
# config/ holds the extension env file and the proxy TOMLs, which carry indexer DB
# credentials in a real working copy. Both env spellings, at every depth.
.env
.env.*
*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
config/

# VCS metadata, editor/tooling state, CI definitions
.git
.gitignore
.gitleaks.toml
.github/
.claude/
.superpowers/
**/.DS_Store

# go.work is generated by scripts/start-services.sh for USE_LOCAL_SIBLINGS and its `use`
# entries are host paths. `go` discovers it by walking up from the module directory, so a
# copy of it inside the image would redirect the build at directories that are not there.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Solidity sources, Foundry config and build products: contracts are compiled on the host
# and deployed by scripts/, never from inside an image.
foundry.toml
contracts/
test/
out/
cache/
results/
testdata/

# Documentation, host-side tooling, and the build definitions themselves. These are the
# top-level spellings, so go/Dockerfile* and go/README.md do stay in the context — they are
# small, and no COPY in any dockerfile names them.
*.md
docs/
testing/
scripts/
proxy/
tools/
docker-compose*.yaml
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore

# Host-built binary committed for convenience; the image builds its own from go/cmd/.
# Spelled as an exact path: `**/start-tee` would also match the go/cmd/start-tee sources.
go/start-tee

# Large, host-dependent dependency trees. Language source directories themselves are NOT
# excluded here: this file is the fallback for whichever dockerfile is selected, and a
# python/ or typescript/ build would need its own sources. Only go/Dockerfile.dockerignore,
# which applies to the Go image alone, excludes the other languages outright.
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/dist/
